A||||24||87FieroGTx||Stock 85GT vs 86 5.0  5 speed Stang||||14||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||11-20-2001||01:03 PM|||| This was the best street race I've ever been in.<P> I was at my sisters house for a pre thanksgiving dinner and my sisters best friends husband pulled up in a rusty but nice 86 Mustang GT 5 speed with almost no exhaust! We get to talking about our cars he's a great guy (A little misinformed but nice) <P> So he asks if I want to see him do a burnout and the "GUY" that I am I say hell yah! Well five 100 feet blackmarks later he asks to see my car do one. I was tempted to go get my  good GT out of storage but I finally decide to just tell him my winter car can hardly chirp them, he starts laughing and saying the usual things.<P> Well we talk a bit more and he lets me drive his Stang (I have to admit I liked spinning the tires and the raw power/sound of the 5.0<P> Ok.. to the race, We are all leaving and he says how about a race (keep in mind this is my winter beater so it's mostly stock(K&N) with heavy snow tires but I say lets do it!<P> The first time we go from my sisters house to the X roads, I power brake to 2500rpm he revs it to about 5k and drops the clutch needless to say I pull him easy and win.<P> When we get to the stop sign I tell him "Try not to spin your tires" rev to say 2k and ease into it.<P> The second race he does what I said and doesn't spin at all we stay side by side all the way up to 75mph then I let off.<P> The third race were going up hill and even know he eases into it he spins BAD!<P> The 4th time He launches perfect and gets out in front of me and Wins.<P> All in all it was a very fun night and I gained a new respect for stock Fieros and 5.0s alike.<P> <BR>Admittedly he wasn't the best driver but it was FUN and to me that's all that maters.<P>Oh.. And these races were out in the middle of nowhere.<P> <P> PS. Anyone know how much power a 86 5 speed 5.0 puts out? And there 0-60 / 1/4?<P> <P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||banditbalz||11-20-2001||01:30 PM||||'86 was the first year fuel injection was offered in 5.O mustang. Rated at 225bhp and 300lb/ft torque. 0-60 in the neighbourhood of 7 seconds with the 5 speed (Borg Warner)I believe. They outweigh Fiero's by 300-400 lbsand suffer higher driveline losses. This coupled with the fact 5.O engines were overated from the factory give Fiero's nice competition!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackStang95||11-20-2001||01:49 PM||||Yeah those numbers are right.  They got faster a bit later in the 80's (mid 6's 0-60, high 14's 1/4).  The 86 fiero gt got 0-60 in the 8 second range with the 5 speed, which is a heck of an accomplishment with 140hp.  Sounds like you had a lot of fun.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't understand what "over-rated from the factory" means though...ford said 225 and that's what it had..how is that an over-rating?  Or were you just trying to take a shot at stangs?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||11-20-2001||02:04 PM||||225hp is about right... The motors were actually under-rated in the early 90's. Sold as 215hp but they were still around 225.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||banditbalz||11-20-2001||02:54 PM||||BlackStang95, I have respect for the 5.O series Mustang's. Cheap fun, best bang for the buck (even today). Check out '93 and on 5.0 specs. That's a big 215bhp posted by Ford. I don't understand the reasoning, but FoMoCo had previously posted 225bhp. <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000005||banditbalz||11-20-2001||03:11 PM||||Only 205hp, overrated by 20hp according to Car and Driver, October 1992. I have other articles that prove the same point. I am NOT going to start looking through the hundreds of car magazines that support this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> Here's what I found...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mustangr.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/over.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||99BlackZ||11-20-2001||09:30 PM||||Sorry guys, but; 86GT Mustangs are only rated at 200hp.  They used swirl combustion heads to increase mpg and the fuel injection system was a restriction.  They upped them to 225hp the following year as they went back to the E7 heads and a little freer breathing FI.  Actually, the 225 was about accurate for 87's to 88's with the speed density.  As they went to mass air and made some other changes throughout the years, then you get the downgrade to 205hp.||||reg||7
Z||000007||Fformula88||11-20-2001||09:41 PM||||Lets all play nice guys.  The proof is in the pudding and on this night the 86 Stang GT and the V6 Fiero are about dead even, each one gaining at least one win!<P>Although I do not have a ton of proof, I bet horsepower figures are often misrepresented.  I do remember reading some articles in Motor Trend and the like stating they thought GM had the LS! V8 in Camaro and Trans Am rated wrong.... although I do not remember ever seeing a dyno on one.<P>I cannot believe your 85 GT won't spin its tires!  My father's 85 SE 2m6 will spin the rears like crazy with the 4-spd tranny!  Maybe its got something to do with those snow tires?  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||11-20-2001||10:23 PM|||| Both of my cars are Autos.<P> I can get them to spin/chirp for maybe 1/2 a second in a straight line but that's it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> My summer car has almost 275hp with NOS and will lay a nice patch <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> Next summer when I do my engine swap in my good car I'm going with a 286? 5 speed and eather a 3.8 turbo/supercharged or a 3.4/3.5 TDC. <P> I'm actually thinking about selling my TA and buying an old 5.0!<P> Don't worry though, I will NEVER sell my Fiero!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||2.8-4spd||11-21-2001||08:31 PM||||I think my 85 2.8 4 speed is a great car, but it will not beat my 86 mustang gt 5 speed in a drag race line||||reg||1
Z||000010||yo_sweet||11-21-2001||09:15 PM||||and 87 GTA Transam with a 350 tuned port fuel injected 350 will hand 80s stock rustangs there a$$es any day!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||11-21-2001||11:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2.8-4spd:<BR><B>I think my 85 2.8 4 speed is a great car, but it will not beat my 86 mustang gt 5 speed in a drag race line</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How convenient... <P>One of the first races I ever had was with my cousins 86 GT (18,000 mile car) I took him by about a car length with my 4spd when it was stock. The last go I had was with a later 80's 5ltr hatch at the corel Center , we dragged across the parking lot (anyone who has seen this lot knows it's huge) We hit around 90 and I was about 1/2 car length ahead<P>Not too shabby for a 2.8 with minimal mods.<P>I raced an 85 GT (carb'd) I smoked him.... 160hp 5.0ltr.<P>Nice lookin car with the red and flat black hood accents though...<P>The kind to stay away from are late 80's LX's ..the GT's have 0 to 60 of 7 sec ..all that body cladding makes them heavy<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000012||2.8-4spd||11-22-2001||03:32 PM||||no slushbox 3700 pound gta ever beat my 86 gt mustang, And my carbed 85 capri GS 5.0, 5 speed is rated at 210 hp stock, not 165||||reg||12
Z||000013||lou||11-22-2001||05:50 PM||||My stock 87 5 speed 5.7 tpi T/A has consistently beat mid to late 1980's Mustangs at Moroso. When I had a stock 85 Fiero gt 4 speed it also beat out the stock mid  80's Mustangs at Moroso.  The slips don't lie, Ford does lie about horsepower just look at what happened with the 320 HP  Cobras !  I believe that 85 GT is the fastest year for a Fiero as my 87 and 88 GT s' are not quite as fast. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||2.8-4spd||11-22-2001||08:09 PM||||Lou, This will be my last post on this. Could you always get the five speed with the 350 tpi? My understanding was that you could only get the five speed with the 305, but i could be wrong. I have not had my 85 2.8,4 speed fiero to drag strip, but i know it will not beat my 86 mustang gt 5 speed. But i did not buy my fiero for that reason anyway. I love it, and think one of the best cars I have owned, and once it is done it will be the best car I have owned. The reason I responed to the thread was because I own both cars in question, not to start a fight. Since I have been on here I have seen enough of that stuff. Iam just going to be happy with having cars that I love, and be glad that we all have cars we like.  ||||reg||12
Z||000015||BlackStang95||11-22-2001||09:38 PM||||Yeah look at the Cobras, they stopped production the next year and painstakingly repaired every car at great monentary loss until Cobra made every one of its 320 ponies...ford sure does suck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Posted by yosweet:<BR>"and 87 GTA Transam with a 350 tuned port fuel injected 350 will hand 80s stock rustangs there a$$es any day!"<P>1988   Pontiac Firebird Trans Am GTA          7.4            15.9<P>1988   Ford Mustang GT                         6.4           15.0<P><BR>Hell son, 7.4 will barely hand my v-6 stang its ass, 350 or no 350.  Did you say 350 enough times?  You just need to quit posting until you learn more about cars.||||reg||1
