Z||000017||lou||11-22-2001||10:13 PM||||2.8 4sp : No fight intended, the 5 speed (MM5) was available as a late year special order in 87 and dropped for 88.  GTAs with the 5.7 automatic tranny were slower than the 5.0 5 speed trannys. However the 5.7 with the 5 speed was the fastest with 14.6 sec quarter mile times. This car was available through Macho T/A or Asc/Mclaren/Knudsen (Tojan).  Although I do not have my original car I managed to find and buy a Tojan convertible with an automatic a few years back. here is a rather large picture : <A HREF="http://www.4u2buy.com/Fiero/TOJAN.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.4u2buy.com/Fiero/TOJAN.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||BlackStang95||11-23-2001||01:37 AM||||The stang gt's were usually a bit slower than the lx 5.0's too, you pay a price for sweet styling and luxurious interior etc.||||reg||1
Z||000019||GTMike||11-23-2001||01:54 AM||||sweet styling? <p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||watts||11-23-2001||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2.8-4spd:<BR><B>Could you always get the five speed with the 350 tpi? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just so happens that I bought a GTA back in '88.  Wanted the 350/5spd (well, I WANTED a 454 5spd..  ha ha), but....<P>According to the dealer at the time - They had to drop the 350/5spd/T-top option package due to the large number of warranty claims.  The package had too much torque potential and was twisting the bodies enough to crack the t-tops.  So, you could only get a 350 with an automatic.  <P>They must have stiffened up the bodies later on (I guess?), as that package did reappear at some point - before or after the start of the 4th gen bodies I don't know.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||lou||11-23-2001||01:32 PM||||That is correct in 87 the 5.7 speed did flex the unibody to the point that stress cracks did appear, this is why the manual w/the 5.7 was dropped for 88 and came back in 93 after the unibody was re-inforced. The Fiero however was designed to hold up to 500hp  this is why the sunroof provision was left in place and why they also have a 5 star safety rating.  <p>[This message has been edited by lou (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||LoW_KeY||11-23-2001||03:21 PM||||Hehe sweet styling? I think my brothers 88 LX looked no different then GT's. He had a spoiler, I'm mean yeah sure it did look a tad different, but nothing like the coupe fiero to a gt.<P>That's just some styling there.<P>Heck that was the first fast ride I rode in was my brothers stang I was all about getting one when I was 14.  I mean he had some major stuff done to it, but he even told me the fiero would give it one hell of a good race and that was with the 2.8.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Spektrum-87GT||11-23-2001||08:40 PM||||although there isnt a huge difference like the couple to gt... there is still a big difference<P>just look<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598322704" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598322704</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598202502" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598202502</A> <P>gt has different tailight and front bumper cover, ground effects, not sure if the spoiler was an option on the lx<P>but i really like the look of the gt... the lx is just too plain.||||reg||1
Z||000024||87gtfiero||11-23-2001||10:17 PM||||I bought an 87 Fiero GT 5 spd new in 87 and now have an 88 5.0 LX Mustang.The Fiero will NEVER beat a 5.0 stock car to stock car in the 1/4 mile but light to light the Mustang is in trouble on stock tires.I currently run 2.3 60 ft times on street tires(about the same as an S-10 p/u}but I will beat him to the end of the 1/4 by about 3 seconds,I've done it at National Trail Raceway.My Fiero ran 15.7 with a K&N filter only,my 5.0 runs 14.0 at 100 mph.If you want to beat me with a GTA you better get a supercharger or NOS,those cars are too heavy.I would want proof about a 5spd 5.7 I don't think they ever made one from the factory.My 5.0 is fast but I miss my NOS Fiero.||||reg||1
